summary:
  The fold ignores the fence around a deferred settle repair — a waiting
  full-size correction gets clamped back to 60 ms.

history:
  Found on the 2026-08-10 foreign-desk review: with two Bluetooth members
  (or any geometry that would move a BT loopback) the settle road writes
  its full correction to the map and waits for a rebuild to land it. The
  periodic fold rewrites map entries from the DEPLOYED base, so without
  the fence it overwrote the waiting repair with its own 60 ms step some
  eighteen minutes later — the feature's core promise lost silently, on
  desks this one cannot reproduce. The mutant flips the fence's condition,
  the way a hasty refactor would.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
          for (var dm in _settleDeferredMacs)
              if (steps[dm] !== undefined) delete steps[dm];

replace:
          for (var dm in _settleDeferredMacs)
              if (steps[dm] === undefined) delete steps[dm];

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine.qml
  test_a_deferred_settle_repair_is_fenced_from_the_fold: with the fence
  set, three agreeing readings must leave the map at 145; the flipped
  condition folds them in and the compare goes red.
